---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About — Michael Rashkin" description="About Michael Rashkin: population health and nutrition analysis.">
  <section class="container" style="padding-top: 38px;">
    <div class="prose">
      <h1>About Michael Rashkin</h1>
      <p>
        I’m Michael Rashkin. I work at the intersection of nutrition and population health.
        My focus is on how nutrition advice performs in the real world, at scale, across different communities, incentives, and constraints.
        I aim to separate evidence from ideology, label opinion clearly, cite sources, and publish corrections when needed.
      </p>

      <h2>Credentials</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>DHSc (Population Health), Thomas Jefferson University</li>
        <li>MS (Nutrition and Functional Medicine), University of Western States</li>
        <li>Certified Nutrition Specialist (CNS)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What I focus on</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Population-level drivers of nutrition and health outcomes</li>
        <li>Evidence quality and interpretation</li>
        <li>Adherence and behavior in real-world settings</li>
        <li>Food environment and incentives</li>
        <li>Policy tradeoffs and unintended consequences</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How I handle disagreement</h2>
      <p>
        I expect disagreement. If you think I’m wrong, the best place to start is the Evidence section.
        If a factual claim is wrong, I correct it. If a value judgment differs, I say so.
      </p>

      <h2>Media-ready short bio</h2>
      <div class="card">
        Michael Rashkin (DHSc, MS, CNS) analyzes nutrition through a population health lens, focusing on evidence quality,
        real-world adherence, and the policy and incentive structures that shape health outcomes.
      </div>

      <div style="margin-top: 18px;">
        <a class="button" href="/contact">Media and speaking requests</a>
      </div>

      <hr />
      <p class="muted small">
        Starter note: convert this page into a CMS-managed page later if you want.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
